<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">King Xuan of Zhou</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 827–782 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century-bce">9th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">King Xuan of Zhou was the eleventh king of the Western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhou-dynasty">Zhou dynasty</a>, who came to the throne after the Gonghe regency. He restored royal authority, campaigning against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xianyun">Xianyun</a> in the north and the Huai peoples in the south. He reorganised the frontier by moving the Earl of Shen to guard the south and enfeoffed his brother as the first ruler of Zheng in 806 BCE.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/king-xuan-of-zhou.jpg" alt="King Xuan of Zhou" width="320" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:King_Xuan_(monarch_of_the_Zhou_dynasty).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
